$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Quasi-isotropic laminate, single shell element  --  MSC Nastran SOL 101
$
$   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa, density 1.57-9)
$   model : 1 x 1 mm CQUAD4, 4 plies [0/45/-45/90] x 0.125 mm = 0.5 mm
$           membrane only (all rotations and uz fixed), pulled to ux = 0.005 mm
$           -> eps_x = 0.5%, transverse contraction free
$   check : laminate average sigma_x ~= 260.45 MPa, edge reaction ~= 130.23 N
$           (CLT: E_eff = 52090.3 MPa, nu_eff = 0.30686)
$
$   This one is LINEAR (SOL 101) on purpose.  The laminate response at 0.5% strain
$   is linear elastic, so the answer is a closed-form CLT check that every
$   solver in the set must reproduce exactly.
$
$   PCOMP field order is  PID Z0 NSM SB FT TREF GE LAM  -- FT is the FIFTH data
$   field.  Leave FT blank and no failure index is computed at all; the run
$   still succeeds, which is how "no failure reported" gets mistaken for "safe".
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE    = QI laminate 1-element tension (mm-N-tonne-s)
ECHO     = NONE
$
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = pull to eps_x = 0.5 percent
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 2
  DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL
  STRESS(PLOT)       = ALL
  FORCE(PLOT)        = ALL
  SPCFORCES(PLOT)    = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
PARAM,POST,-1
$
$===============================================================================
$ MESH
$===============================================================================
$       ID                      X       Y       Z
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               1.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    3               1.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     1.0     0.0
$
$       EID     PID     G1      G2      G3      G4      THETA
CQUAD4  1       100     1       2       3       4       0.0
$
$===============================================================================
$ LAMINATE
$   PCOMP  PID  Z0  NSM  SB  FT  TREF  GE  LAM
$   then   MIDi Ti  THETAi SOUTi  (two plies per continuation line)
$===============================================================================
PCOMP   100                     60.0    TSAI    20.0
+       1       0.125   0.0     YES     1       0.125   45.0    YES
+       1       0.125   -45.0   YES     1       0.125   90.0    YES
$
$===============================================================================
$ PLY MATERIAL
$   MAT8  MID  E1  E2  NU12  G12  G1Z  G2Z  RHO
$         A1   A2  TREF  Xt  Xc  Yt  Yc  S
$===============================================================================
MAT8    1       135000. 9000.   0.3     5000.   5000.   3500.   1.57-9
+       -0.5-6  28.0-6  20.0    2200.   1400.   60.0    200.0   90.0
$
$===============================================================================
$ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS   (membrane only + enforced displacement)
$===============================================================================
$       SID     C       G1      G2      G3      G4
SPC1    1       1       1       4
SPC1    1       2       1       2
SPC1    1       3456    1       2       3       4
SPC1    1       1       2       3
$
$       SID     G1      C1      D1      G2      C2      D2
SPCD    2       2       1       0.005   3       1       0.005
$
ENDDATA
